# A slice may be empty at either end and may be the whole Binary, which keeps every byte; a start
# below 0 throws, as an end beyond the length and a start after the end do.
bytes := 'héllo'.binary
print bytes.slice(bytes.length, bytes.length).length
print bytes.slice(0, 0).length
whole := bytes.slice(0, bytes.length)
print whole.length
print whole == bytes
print whole.text()!
try
  print bytes.slice(-1, 1).length
catch e: IndexError
  print e.message
